From 2e05db1bb84d8cb2477984343affa31fa2190afb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vibecode-vm <vcvm@servas.ai>
Date: Sat, 16 May 2026 22:22:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(detection): CLO-115 Gradle wiring + namespace
 unification

Wires agents/detection/ into a compilable Kotlin/JVM Gradle module and
finalises the com.example.detectorlab -> com.detectorlab namespace rename
across all probe + test sources.

(a) settings.gradle.kts: declares :detection module pointing at
    agents/detection/. W3 detector-lab (Android app) intentionally not
    registered -- scope-bounded per CTO 2026-05-16.

(b) agents/detection/build.gradle.kts: kotlin("jvm") 1.9.25, JUnit 5 via
    useJUnitPlatform(), kotlinx-coroutines 1.8.1, JVM toolchain 17.
    Custom source set maps the non-standard src/core + src/probes layout
    (preserved to avoid churn). checkNamespace task hooked into :check
    fails the build if 'com.example.detectorlab' regresses into source.

(c) Namespace unified: 14 probe/core .kt files updated, 8 test .kt files
    moved from com/example/detectorlab/ -> com/detectorlab/. Verified:
    grep -rn 'com\.example\.detectorlab' agents/detection/ = 0 matches.

(d) .gitignore: adds .gradle/ + gradle-app.setting (keeps gradle-wrapper.jar
    trackable).

Acceptance (CI-only, runs_on per issue spec):
  gradle :detection:compileKotlin && gradle :detection:test  -> expect exit 0
  gradle :detection:check  -> runs checkNamespace regression guard

Unblocks CLO-113 (TimeSpoofingProbeTest can now compile + run under
this harness).

Refs: CLO-115, CLO-106 (acceptance-evidence gap addressed)

Co-Authored-By: Paperclip <noreply@paperclip.ing>
